// Settings that are specific to your organization. Everything here has a built-in default,
// so a missing file (or a missing line) is fine. Restart the app after editing this file.
//
//   adminAccountSuffix   - how admin accounts are named, e.g. "-admin" for jdoe-admin.
//                          The header dot is green when the app runs as such an account, and c$ Share
//                          opens the profile of the same name without the suffix (C:\Users\jdoe).
//                          "" = no separate admin accounts.
//   directAccessGroup    - name of the DirectAccess / VPN group shown in PC Details and offered by
//                          Add Remote Desktop. Looked up as a local group on the PC first, then in AD.
//   highlightIpPrefixes  - IP addresses starting with one of these show in orange in PC Details
//                          (for example a VPN or guest range); other addresses show in green.
//                          [] = no colouring.
//   uptimeCautionHours   - uptime above this shows in yellow
//   uptimeBadHours       - uptime above this shows in red
//   gpoFreshDays         - Group Policy dates within this many days (today included) show in green, older in red
//   dismSource           - where SFC Scan's DISM /RestoreHealth gets its repair files (DISM's /Source option).
//                          "" = Windows Update / WSUS (the DISM default). Otherwise, as seen from the REMOTE PC:
//                            "wim:D:\\sources\\install.wim:1"           image 1 of a WIM file
//                            "esd:C:\\Sources\\install.esd:6"           image 6 of an ESD file
//                            "C:\\RepairSource\\Windows"                a folder holding a matching Windows install
//                            "wim:\\\\server\\share\\install.wim:1"     a file share
//                          The source must be the same Windows version and build as the PC.
//                          The remote PC reads the source itself, and PowerShell remoting normally can't pass
//                          your logon on to another server. If DISM reports that a file share source can't
//                          be found, copy the files onto the PC and name that local path instead.
//   dismLimitAccess      - true = use only dismSource and never contact Windows Update (/LimitAccess).
//                          Ignored when dismSource is "".
//   scriptTabs           - tabs of the Scripts card, in this order. A category in scripts.json that
//                          isn't listed here is added as an extra tab at the end.
{
  "adminAccountSuffix": "-admin",
  "directAccessGroup": "Direct Access Users",
  "highlightIpPrefixes": [ "105.195." ],
  "uptimeCautionHours": 48,
  "uptimeBadHours": 96,
  "gpoFreshDays": 7,
  "dismSource": "",
  "dismLimitAccess": false,
  "scriptTabs": [ "Testing", "Tools", "Fixes", "GAD", "Utilities", "Installs" ]
}
